  "qualityNotes": [
    "Budapest is the unified city only from 1873-11-17. The separate historical Pest place (GeoNames 3046446, modern PPLX, coordinates 47.5/19.0833333) is shown in the city layer before 1873-11-17 and suppressed from that date by staged temporalEligibility.activeIntervals; Budapest GeoNames 3054643 is suppressed before that date by its existing temporalEligibility.cityEstablishedFromDate. Buda and Óbuda remain linked predecessor settlements, not aliases of Budapest.",
    "Warsaw: 1801 Prussian Warschau/바르샤우, 1807-07-09 Duchy of Warsaw treaty Warszawa/바르샤바, 1868 year-level Russianized administration Варшава, 1917-12-07 Regency Kingdom Polish cabinet Warszawa. English Warsaw remains unchanged; Congress Poland from 1815 is not treated as direct Russian imperial territory. Prague: 1801 German Prag/프라크, 1861-11-01 municipal adoption of Czech Praha/프라하, English Prague unchanged. Neither language transition is construed as a new legal city name. Brussels' concurrent French/Dutch names continue under existing policy.",
    "Athens: selected Ottoman Turkish آتینا / Korean 아티나 from 1801; Greek Ἀθῆναι / Korean 아테네 from 1833-03-31 (Ottoman withdrawal), then Greek Ἀθήνα c. 1976 and Αθήνα c. 1982. English Athens remains unchanged. Korean is the selected native-language pronunciation convention by period, not evidence of contemporary Korean historical usage or an actual city renaming.",
    "Amsterdam is a city point, not its municipality or metro; Brussels city point is distinct from the 19-municipality capital region.",
    "Short displayed text is <=28 Unicode codepoints. Map renderer and production manifest are unchanged.",
    "GeoNames PPLX Pest is a scoped exception to the modern capital PPLC selection: independent historic municipality until 1873, then part of modern Budapest. As of this staged report, runtime label resolver does not consume activeIntervals; the historical display rule is pending runtime integration.",
    "Vienna, Budapest, Amsterdam, and Lisbon now have explicit period ko/en/native names without introducing unsupported naming transitions. Budapest and Pest remain separate historic city IDs before 1873-11-17 and Pest is suppressed as independent city thereafter.",
    "Warsaw and Prague trilingual timelines finalized: 1915 wartime occupation does not prompt a Warsaw name switch; 1894 Prague Czech street-sign directive does not imply a city rename. The 1868 Warsaw transition is approximate year precision. Production runtime and Pest/Budapest historic separation are unchanged."
  ],
